{"name":"Luck of the Irish","hex":"#547839","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"luck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that happens to someone by chance, a chance occurrence.","A favourable chance occurrence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To find something through good fortune; used with into, on, onto or upon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luck"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Luck of the Irish (1920 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Luck of the Irish is a 1920 American silent drama film directed by Allan Dwan. It is based on the 1917 novel The Luck of the Irish by Harold MacGrath. The film stars James Kirkwood Sr., Anna Q. Nilsson, Harry Northrup, Ward Crane, Ernest Butterworth Jr., and Gertrude Messinger. The film was released on January 5, 1920, by Realart Pictures Corporation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/The_Luck_of_the_Irish_%281920%29_-_Ad_1.jpg/330px-The_Luck_of_the_Irish_%281920%29_-_Ad_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Luck_of_the_Irish_(1920_film)","wikidata":"Q3988132"},{"title":"The Luck of the Irish (1936 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Luck of the Irish is a British drama film directed by Donovan Pedelty, who also co-wrote the screenplay, and starring Richard Hayward and Kay Walsh. It is based on a novel by Victor Haddick."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Luck_of_the_Irish_(1936_film)","wikidata":"Q7749142"},{"title":"Luck","blocks":[{"text":"Luck is a phenomenon or belief that humans may associate with experiencing improbable events, especially improbably positive or negative events.\nPhilosophical naturalism, eschewing any supernatural explanations, might suggest that positive or negative events may happen at any time, and that even improbable events can happen by random chance.\nIn this view, the epithet \"lucky\" or \"unlucky\" is a descriptive label that refers to an event's positivity, negativity, or improbability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Four-leaf_clover.jpg/330px-Four-leaf_clover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luck","wikidata":"Q1970348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg/250px-1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg/250px-1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1927 advertisement for lucky jewellery. \"Why Be Unlucky?\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Maneki_neko_with_7_Lucky_Gods_by_OiMax_in_Asakusa%2C_Tokyo.jpg/500px-Maneki_neko_with_7_Lucky_Gods_by_OiMax_in_Asakusa%2C_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Maneki_neko_with_7_Lucky_Gods_by_OiMax_in_Asakusa%2C_Tokyo.jpg/1280px-Maneki_neko_with_7_Lucky_Gods_by_OiMax_in_Asakusa%2C_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Maneki_neko_with_7_Lucky_Gods_by_OiMax_in_Asakusa%2C_Tokyo.jpg/500px-Maneki_neko_with_7_Lucky_Gods_by_OiMax_in_Asakusa%2C_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maneki-neko with Seven Lucky gods","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManeki_neko_with_7_Lucky_Gods_by_OiMax_in_Asakusa%2C_Tokyo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm